  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef has NNN magic spells. The iii-th spell has a volatility of ViV_iVi​ and a strength of AiA_iAi​.\n\nWhen spells iii and jjj (1≤i&lt;j≤N1 \\leq i \\lt j \\leq N1≤i&lt;j≤N) are activated together, they merge to form a single spell of strength (Ai×Vj+Vi×Aj)(A_i\\times V_j + V_i\\times A_j)(Ai​×Vj​+Vi​×Aj​).\n\nWhat's the **maximum** possible strength of a spell Chef can obtain by activating exactly two of his spells?\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN, the number of spells.\nThe next NNN lines describe the spells. The iii-th of them contains two space-separated integers ViV_iVi​ and AiA_iAi​ — the volatility and strength of the iii-th spell.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the maximum possible power of a combined spell.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\leq T \\leq 1001≤T≤100",
      "2≤N≤1002 \\leq N \\leq 1002≤N≤100",
      "1≤Ai,Vi≤10001 \\leq A_i, V_i \\leq 10001≤Ai​,Vi​≤1000"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n2\n1 10\n5 5\n4\n4 7\n8 9\n10 2\n6 6\n4\n35 45\n5 50\n50 5\n45 35",
        "output": "55\n106\n3250",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: There are only two spells. Combining them results in a spell of strength 1×5+5×10=551\\times 5 + 5\\times 10 = 551×5+5×10=55.\nTest case 222: It's optimal to choose the second and third spells. Combining them results in a spell of strength 8×2+10×9=1068\\times 2 + 10\\times 9 = 1068×2+10×9=106.\nTest case 333: It's optimal to choose the first and fourth spells. Combining them results in a spell of strength 45×45+35×35=325045\\times 45 + 35\\times 35 = 325045×45+35×35=3250."
      }
    ]
  },
